window.docContents[243].resolve({"/Hoare/#Hoare-Logic--Hoare___-Hoare-Logic___-Part-I--Assertions":{"contents":"An assertion is a logical claim about the state of a program's\nmemory -- formally, a predicate of States.\n\nopen scoped MyGetElem\n\nabbrev Assertion := State → Prop\n\n\nHIDE: MRC'20: pulled up these examples from the quiz/optional\nexercise so that there would be some modeling of the kinds of\nanswers we expect.\n\nFor example,\n\n* fun st => st[X] = 3 holds for states st in which value of X\n  is 3,* fun st => True hold for all states, and* fun st => False holds for no states.\n\nParaphrase the following assertions in English (i.e., say\nwhich states satisfy them)(A) fun st => st[X] ≤ st[Y](B) fun st => st[X] = 3 ∨ st[X] ≤ st[Y](C) fun st => st[Z] * st[Z] ≤ st[X] ∧ ¬ ((st[Z] + 1) * (st[Z] + 1) ≤ st[X])\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Hoare Logic\u0009Hoare: Hoare Logic, Part I","header":"4.1. Assertions","id":"/Hoare/#Hoare-Logic--Hoare___-Hoare-Logic___-Part-I--Assertions"}});